  "result": "The fix works. All tests pass in any order now.\nI changed one line of app code and no tests. Nothing else is needed from you.\n\n**Cause:** The bug is in `src/config/options.mjs`. `resolveOptions` used `Object.assign(DEFAULTS, overrides)`. That writes each tenant's options into the shared `DEFAULTS` object. Here is the chain:\n\n- An options test runs `globex`, whose `quoteTtlDays` is 30.\n- After that, every tenant gets 30 days, not 14.\n- The quote test then fails: `2026-04-01` came back, but `2026-03-16` was expected.\n- Run alone, nothing changes the defaults first, so it passes.\n\n**Fix:** It now builds a new object each time, so the defaults stay the same:\n\n```js\nreturn { ...DEFAULTS, ...overrides };\n```\n\n**Checks:**\n- `npm test` gives 46 pass, 0 fail.\n- Reverse file order gives 46 pass, 0 fail.\n- 8 random file orders all gave 0 fail.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
